# Oct 11 — Phase 1: Full Scan and In-Memory HashMap Index

This is the Phase 1 milestone that was skipped when the project moved ahead to
the in-memory B+ tree. The purpose is to understand why an index is useful
before implementing a more complicated tree or disk format.

This milestone is entirely in memory. Do not add files, `FileChannel`, binary
serialization, caching, locking, or B+ tree code here.

